         <t:abstract>
             <t:p>The monastic genealogy of <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9162TaklaHa">St Takla Hāymānot</t:persName> that shows
             his spiritual descendance from <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS1962Anthony">St Anthony</t:persName> and tells about his disciples
             and their spiritual successors. In part based on <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3973GadlaT">the Vita of Takla Hāymānot</t:ref>,
             a kind of monastic history of Ethiopia in the version of <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0341DL">the monastery Dabra Libānos</t:placeName>.
             Mostly follows <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3973GadlaT">Gadla Takla Hāymānot (general record)</t:ref>.
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
